Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-07-29
Subject: Count optcse references as pointer-sized integers
License: expat

`refs` is a TFPList only to reuse its indexed storage.  Its items are
reference counts encoded in pointer-sized slots; they are never addresses
and are never dereferenced.  Incrementing a Pointer therefore applies
pointer arithmetic to integer data and misstates the operation.  Convert
through PtrUInt so the count arithmetic is explicit and follows the target
pointer width, then convert back for TFPList storage.

--- a/compiler/optcse.pas
+++ b/compiler/optcse.pas
@@ -236,6 +236,6 @@
                     else
                       plists(arg)^.equalto[plists(arg)^.nodelist.count-1]:=pointer(ptrint(i));
-                    plists(arg)^.refs[i]:=pointer(plists(arg)^.refs[i])+1;
+                    plists(arg)^.refs[i]:=pointer(ptruint(plists(arg)^.refs[i])+1);
                     { tree has been found, no need to search further,
                       sub-trees have been added by the first occurence of
                       the tree already }
